{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:42441853 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:42441853 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"42441853","source":"MED","pmid":"42441853","pmcid":"PMC13389597","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13389597"]},"doi":"10.1073/pnas.2602557123","title":"Evolutionary innovation through fusion of sequences from across the tree of life.","authorString":"Kapoor RR, Schwager EE, Phuangphong S, Rivard EL, Kuyyamudi C, Ghosh S, Ronai I, Extavour CG.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Kapoor RR","lastName":"Kapoor","firstName":"Rishabh R","initials":"RR","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3082-1507"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Systems, Synthetic, and Quantitative Biology Program, Harvard Medical School, Harvard University, Boston, MA 02115."}]}},{"fullName":"Schwager EE","lastName":"Schwager","firstName":"Evelyn E","initials":"EE","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"HHMI, Chevy Chase, MD 20815."},{"affiliation":"Department of Organismic and Evolutionary Biology, Harvard University, Cambridge, MA 02138."}]}},{"fullName":"Phuangphong S","lastName":"Phuangphong","firstName":"Supanat","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0003-5251-5858"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Organismic and Evolutionary Biology, Harvard University, Cambridge, MA 02138."}]}},{"fullName":"Rivard EL","lastName":"Rivard","firstName":"Emily L","initials":"EL","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Molecular and Cellular Biology, Harvard University, Cambridge, MA 02138."}]}},{"fullName":"Kuyyamudi C","lastName":"Kuyyamudi","firstName":"Chandrashekar","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"HHMI, Chevy Chase, MD 20815."},{"affiliation":"Department of Organismic and Evolutionary Biology, Harvard University, Cambridge, MA 02138."}]}},{"fullName":"Ghosh S","lastName":"Ghosh","firstName":"Suhrid","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6110-0169"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"HHMI, Chevy Chase, MD 20815."},{"affiliation":"Department of Organismic and Evolutionary Biology, Harvard University, Cambridge, MA 02138."}]}},{"fullName":"Ronai I","lastName":"Ronai","firstName":"Isobel","initials":"I","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1658-857X"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"HHMI, Chevy Chase, MD 20815."},{"affiliation":"Department of Organismic and Evolutionary Biology, Harvard University, Cambridge, MA 02138."}]}},{"fullName":"Extavour CG","lastName":"Extavour","firstName":"Cassandra G","initials":"CG","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2922-5855"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"HHMI, Chevy Chase, MD 20815."},{"affiliation":"Department of Organismic and Evolutionary Biology, Harvard University, Cambridge, MA 02138."},{"affiliation":"Department of Molecular and Cellular Biology, Harvard University, Cambridge, MA 02138."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6110-0169"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1658-857X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2922-5855"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3082-1507"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0003-5251-5858"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["related_data","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"29","volume":"123","journalIssueId":4227232,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Jul","monthOfPublication":7,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A","title":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","essn":"1091-6490","issn":"0027-8424","nlmid":"7505876","isoabbreviation":"Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-07-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"e2602557123","abstractText":"Novel genes arise through multiple mechanisms, including gene duplication, gene fusion, and horizontal gene transfer (HGT). While HGT has increasingly been documented in animals, the posttransfer evolutionary fate of horizontally acquired genes is less well understood. We hypothesized that fusion with endogenous sequences in animal genomes might generate what we call \"HGT-chimeras\": genes with regions of nonmetazoan and metazoan descent in the same open reading frame. To test this hypothesis, we developed a molecular phylogenetics pipeline that enables the identification of HGT-chimeras. We applied our pipeline to 319 high-quality annotated arthropod genomes and uncovered a high-confidence set of 274 HGT-chimeras corresponding to 104 independent origination events across diverse arthropods. HGT-chimeras contain intervals acquired from across the tree of life, and many likely originated via a gene duplication-based mechanism. To assess whether HGT-chimeras might be functionally important, we performed RT-PCR and Sanger sequencing of tissues from 20 arthropod species predicted to harbor HGT-chimeras in their genome. We found evidence for the expression of contiguous chimeric messenger RNA transcripts (mRNAs) for 36 of 41 tested HGT-chimeras across 18 of 20 different tested species. We also found evidence that HGT-chimeras evolve under purifying selection and have acquired potentially functional domain architectures, consistent with the hypothesis that these genes are in active use and may participate in diverse biological processes. These results illuminate an underappreciated combinatorial mechanism underlying the origin of novel genes across the largest animal phylum, and suggest that interdomain sequence fusion can play important roles in animal biology and evolution.","affiliation":"Systems, Synthetic, and Quantitative Biology Program, Harvard Medical School, Harvard University, Boston, MA 02115.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Life Sciences Research Foundation","grantId":"n/a","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NSF (NSF)","grantId":"DMS-1764269","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Herchel Smith Graduate Fellowship","grantId":"n/a","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NSF | NSF Graduate Research Fellowship Program (GRFP)","grantId":"2023356057","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Life Sciences Research Foundation (LSRF)","grantId":"n/a","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Harvard University","grantId":"n/a","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NSF | NSF Graduate Research Fellowship Program","grantId":"2023356057","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NSF","grantId":"DMS-1764269","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Human Frontier Science Program (HFSP)","grantId":"RGP0041/2022","orderIn":0},{"agency":"HHMI","grantId":"n/a","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Human Frontier Science Program","grantId":"RGP0041/2022","orderIn":0},{"agency":"HHMI (HHMI)","grantId":"n/a","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Harvard University (Harvard)","grantId":"n/a","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Arthropods","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CL","qualifierName":"classification"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Gene Fusion"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Evolution, Molecular"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Phylogeny"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Gene Duplication"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Gene Transfer, Horizontal","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Genome"}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Gene fusion","Molecular evolution","Horizontal gene transfer","Arthropods"]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2602557123"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13389597"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13389597?pdf=render"}]},"commentCorrectionList":{"commentCorrection":[{"source":"PPR","id":"PPR1074229","type":"Preprint in","note":"Link created based on a title-first author match","orderIn":10002}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["doi"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2026-07-14","dateOfCreation":"2026-07-13","dateOfRevision":"2026-09-22","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-07-13","firstPublicationDate":"2026-07-13","firstIndexDate":"2026-07-15","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-09-03","hasEvaluations":"N"}]}}